$\mathcal{P}$ is not a Hopf algebra, but it turns out that there is a natural
Hopf comodule structure on the ring $\mathcal{P}$ over the Hopf algebra
$\mathcal{RP}$.

\begin{prop}
Formula
$$
\Delta_{\mathcal{RP}} P=\sum\limits_{F\subseteq P}F\otimes(P/F)
$$
defines a natural graded right Hopf comodule structure
$\Delta_{\mathcal{RP}}\colon\mathcal{P}\to\mathcal{P}\otimes\mathcal{RP}$ on
the ring $\mathcal{P}$ over the Hopf algebra $\mathcal{RP}$.
\end{prop}
